Package: bootmakr
Title: Bootstrap Inference for Sensemakr Sensitivity Analysis
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jesper N.", "Wulff", email = "jwulff@econ.au.dk", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Sirio", "Lonati", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Wraps sensemakr sensitivity analysis in a bootstrap loop to produce
    bootstrap standard errors, confidence intervals, and p-values for adjusted
    treatment effect estimates. Supports multiple kd values, one-way and two-way
    cluster bootstrap (the latter via the Cameron, Gelbach & Miller (2011)
    subtractive variance estimator with a normal-approximation CI), stratified
    bootstrap, weights, convergence diagnostics, and visualization. Also
    reports the strength of the benchmark, and of the omitted variable it
    implies, as partial R-squared values and partial correlations.
